0 Gills finely dentate. Metuloids absent. Cap 1.5-5(-11) cm, yellow to ochraceous, later whitish, reniform to cupulate; gills white to yellowish, anastomosing; stem very short or absent, central to eccentric; sp-print pale ochraceous; smell strong of aniseed. Sp 7-8 * 3.5-4 µm. - Solitary on trunks of Salix", autumn. D&D 17, M&J I Panus 1. D: EJyl (Silkeborg, Rold Skov). N: 1-2 s r. S: 1-3 r. F: 2-3 V, EH, OP. 034615110 L. suavissimus Fr. (Panus s. (Fr.) Sing.)0
